# cmux dependency pin (the "required version" record).
#
# cmux is an EXTERNAL, unvendored macOS app (/Applications/cmux.app) that this
# repo's hooks and launchers introspect and drive. It has no in-repo binary and
# no upstream version lock, which is why the dependency-map flags it as the
# highest-risk dependency (finding 10). This file is the durable pin: the
# minimum cmux version the in-repo consumers have been verified against.
#
# cmux-preflight.sh reads the FIRST non-comment, non-blank line below as the
# required MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH and refuses (fail-closed) when the live cmux is
# missing or older. Bump this line when you re-verify the consumers against a
# newer cmux (see reference_cmux_dependency.md for the update procedure).
#
# Verified against: cmux 0.64.20 (build 100) on 2026-07-26.
0.64.20
